{"id":"NCT06423911","title":"Study of Olverembatinib (HQP1351) in Patients With CML-CP","official":"A Global, Multicenter, Open Label, Randomized, Phase 3 Registrational Study of Olverembatinib (HQP1351) in Patients With Chronic Phase Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML-CP)","summary":"Study comparing efficacy and safety of olverembatinib (investigational arm) vs. bosutinib (control arm) in patients with CML-CP (Part A). Study will also evaluate efficacy and safety of olverembatinib (single-arm) in CML-CP patients with T315I mutation (Part B).\n\nPatients who meet ELN 2025 failure criteria while receiving bosutinib in Part A may be able to receive olverembatinib in crossover follow-on study.","conditions":["Chronic Myeloid Leukemia","CML","CML, Chronic Phase"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"olverembatinib"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Bosutinib"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria\n\nPatients eligible for inclusion in this study must meet all of the following criteria:\n\n1. Age ≥ 18 years old\n2. Diagnosis of CML-CP\n3. Part A: Previously treated with at least two approved TKIs; Part B: T315I mutation at screening and previously treated with at least one approved TKI, with no other effective and/or tolerable therapies available\n4. Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status (PS) ≤ 2\n5. Patient has adequate organ function\n\nExclusion Criteria\n\nPatients eligible for this study must not meet any of the following criteria:\n\n1. For Part A only: T315I or V299L mutation at any time prior to starting study treatment\n2. Active infection that requires systemic drug therapy\n3. Impairment of gastrointestinal (GI) function or GI disease that may significantly alter absorption of study drugs\n4. Previous treatment with or known / suspected hypersensitivity to olverembatinib or any of its excipients\n5. Previous treatment with or known / suspected hypersensitivity to bosutinib or any of its excipients\n6. Pregnant or nursing (lactating) women","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":333,"start":"2024-02-05","pcd":"2027-06-30","upd":"2026-09-15","sponsor":"Ascentage Pharma Group Inc.","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Ascentage Clinical Operations · 301-291-5658 · clinical-trials@ascentage.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1044","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35249","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1112","city":"Anchorage","pr":"Alaska","zip":"99508","s":"R","lat":61.2181,"lon":-149.9003,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1111","city":"Goodyear","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85338","s":"R","lat":33.4353,"lon":-112.3582,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1062","city":"Duarte","pr":"California","zip":"91010","s":"R","lat":34.1394,"lon":-117.9773,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1099","city":"Irvine","pr":"California","zip":"92618","s":"R","lat":33.6695,"lon":-117.8231,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1075","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92037","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1100","city":"Long Beach","pr":"California","zip":"90813","s":"R","lat":33.767,"lon":-118.1892,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1059","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90024","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1121","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95817","s":"R","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1109","city":"Upland","pr":"California","zip":"91786","s":"R","lat":34.0975,"lon":-117.6484,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1045","city":"Augusta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30912","s":"R","lat":33.471,"lon":-81.9748,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site #1110","city":"Newnan","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30265","s":"R","lat":33.3807,"lon":-84.7997,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative S